{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>כלו</b> — Some say: then the prayers of the son of Jesse are ended. And some say: כי כלו — like כללו יפייך (your beauty encompasses all), and this is not correct. And R. Judah HaLevi said: because it is the end of the book, the first scribe wrote so, just as we write, 'Blessed is He who gives strength to the weary.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 72, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:04.348144424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}